{
  "name": "chandlery",
  "version": 1,
  "introduced_by": "gannet",
  "notes": "A ship chandler's store on Front Street: 9 m by 15 m, two storeys under a steep shingled gable, cream clapboard on a granite course, gable end to the street (front local -Z) with a double green door between two big shop windows, a loading door above with a hoist beam and block, a brick chimney and hearth at the back, shelves, counter, casks, rope and crates on both floors, stair on the west wall. Carves its interior.",
